bibliograph-worker (0.7.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.7.4: publishing outranks hydration.

    - Graphile runs jobs in ascending `(priority, run_at)` order and every job
      was priority 0, so ~1,400 due `catalog.genres` jobs starved the
      per-minute `pds-publish` cron: with the PDS back up, the outbox grew and
      `pds_cids` stayed flat because the cron job's `run_at` was newer than the
      whole backlog.
    - `pds-publish` is priority -10; edge-triggered enrichment stays at 0; the
      sweeps' per-edition work is 100, since one edition's genre or cover is
      not urgent and its ledger retries it.
    - `0031` replaces the three claim functions with the priority and
      re-prioritises work already queued under the old policy, skipping itself
      where graphile's schema is absent.

