bibliograph-worker (0.4.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.4.1: a deadlocked ingest transaction is retried instead of failing the
    task.

    - `ingestCandidate` retries SQLSTATE `40P01` (deadlock) and `40001`
      (serialization failure) up to three attempts with jittered backoff. Every
      statement it runs is an upsert or an `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`, so a
      rolled-back attempt leaves nothing behind. Two candidates naming the same
      publisher took its row locks in different orders and deadlocked in
      `linkPublisher`, which crash-looped the worker until systemd's start limit
      gave up. No SQL change.

